# Slab S1, span moment

One-way slab, 1 m strip. Concrete C30/37, reinforcement B500B.
Design moment from the frame analysis.

```calc
m_Ed = 60 kNm/m       # per metre width
b    = 1000 mm        # strip width
M_Ed = m_Ed b to kNm
h    = 250 mm
c_nom = 30 mm
```

## Materials

```calc
f_ck = 30 MPa
f_ctm = 2.9 MPa
alpha_cc = 0.85
gamma_c = 1.5
f_cd = alpha_cc f_ck / gamma_c        # 3.1.6 (3.15)

f_yk = 500 MPa
gamma_s = 1.15
f_yd = f_yk / gamma_s
```

## Reinforcement

Bottom bars ⌀12 c/c 150.

```calc
phi = 12 mm
s   = 150 mm
A_s = pi phi^2 / 4 * b / s to mm^2
d   = h - c_nom - phi / 2
```

## Bending resistance, 6.1

Rectangular stress block, λ = 0.8, η = 1.0 for f_ck ≤ 50 MPa.

```calc
lambda = 0.8
eta    = 1.0
x   = A_s f_yd / (lambda eta f_cd b)
x / d
z   = d - lambda x / 2
M_Rd = A_s f_yd z to kNm
check M_Ed <= M_Rd
```

Ductility: x/d ≤ 0.45 for C30/37 without redistribution.

```calc
check x / d <= 0.45
```

## Minimum reinforcement, 9.2.1.1

```calc
A_s_min = max(0.26 f_ctm / f_yk b d, 0.0013 b d) to mm^2    # (9.1N)
check A_s >= A_s_min
```

## Summary

Utilization {M_Ed / M_Rd}; ⌀12 c/c 150 bottom is sufficient for the span moment.
